Offsets: where the faces beyond two consecutive edges of a face meet along
a tangential edge, the images of those edges on the face's offset are not
intersected with each other: their common vertex is where each crosses
the offset of the tangential edge (mitcad#1199).

The case: a loft from a polygon to a circle (BRepOffsetAPI_ThruSections)
whose circle's seam falls on a side of the polygon, offset inwards closed.
The loft splits that side at its middle, so it becomes two faces tangent
all along the edge between them (the faces' normals agree there within
1e-14). Their offsets share that edge's offset. At each end of the edge,
BRepOffset_Inter2d::ConnexIntByInt walks the wire of the end face (the
polygon's or the circle's) and intersects the images of its consecutive
edges on the end face's offset; at the split the two images are the
curves where the two halves' offsets cut it, and they are tangent there.
Their intersection (RefEdgeInter, a 2D intersection of two B-splines) was
ill-conditioned: 2.7 micrometres off along them for a square to a circle
of radius 15 at 1 mm, 7 at the circle's end. The walks of the two halves
find the same vertex where each image crosses the offset of the tangential
edge, transversally and exactly; FuseVertices merged the three into one
whose tolerance covered the points but kept a parameter on an edge from
the ill-conditioned intersection, so that the checker found the vertex off
its curve (BRepCheck_InvalidPointOnCurveOnSurface): the offset invalid at
most thicknesses, its volume up to 2 cubic millimetres off where it passed.

ConnexIntByInt now skips that intersection (the new MeetAlongTangentEdge
and IsAnalyticOn): only where the two edges' common vertex is a vertex of
three edges, the third tangential all along it (the analysis's
ChFiDS_Tangential, a single interval) with the faces beyond the two edges
on its two sides, both edges have images, and the images' curves on the
offset face are not both lines or conics, whose tangent intersections
the 2D intersector computes exactly (a rounding between planes cut by a
plane is as before). Every other intersection is as before. The offsets
are valid single solids, the inner walls the thickness from the outer ones
within 1e-6 mm, of the volume of the same loft with the seam on a corner
(no side split) within 3e-5 of it.
